  "reason": "With no prior evidence, the key uncertainty is which combination of encoders and fusion strategy yields the strongest multimodal performance. This experiment tests a configuration using the most capable components: scgpt (a pretrained single-cell foundation model likely to capture rich biological structure in RNA) paired with ImageNet-pretrained ViT-L (the strongest available image encoder), multiprofile (to capture diverse cellular states), avgpool (a robust, low-variance aggregation that avoids overfitting risk of transformer), and concat fusion (a simple, well-understood baseline). This establishes a strong baseline accuracy and simultaneously provides information on whether the learned RNA encoder (scgpt) and the ViT-L image encoder are effective, which will guide subsequent experiments toward exploring scvi_n200/pca_n2000 alternatives, transformer aggregation, weighted fusion, or singleprofile variants. As experiment 1 of 10, selecting the most well-motivated strong configuration maximizes the chance of a high early baseline while reducing uncertainty about the encoder choices."
}

